---
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
const steps = [
  { t: 'Requirement assessment', d: 'Understand product specifications, quantity, destination, timeline and commercial expectations.', out: 'A written requirement brief' },
  { t: 'Market benchmarking', d: 'Assess relevant market references and comparable supplier quotations.', out: 'A benchmark you approve' },
  { t: 'Supplier identification and evaluation', d: 'Identify potential suppliers and assess their business credentials, documentation, capabilities and commercial suitability.', out: 'A compared shortlist' },
  { t: 'Negotiation and sample coordination', d: 'Compare offers, negotiate commercial terms and coordinate product samples and agreed quality checks.', out: 'Negotiated terms and samples' },
  { t: 'Procurement and delivery coordination', d: 'Support the agreed procurement process with the buyer, supplier and relevant inspection, logistics and documentation partners.', out: 'Coordinated order follow-up' },
];
---
<section class="section section--paper" id="process">
  <div class="container grid">
    <div class="side">
      <SectionHead index="03" label="How procurement works" title="Five stages. <em>One accountable desk.</em>">
        <p>Each stage has a defined scope and a tangible result, agreed with you before the work starts.</p>
      </SectionHead>
    </div>

    <ol class="steps" role="list">
      {steps.map((s, i) => (
        <li data-reveal>
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">0{i + 1}</span>
          <div>
            <h3>{s.t}</h3>
            <p class="muted">{s.d}</p>
            <p class="out"><span>Result</span> {s.out}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <p class="note clar" data-reveal>
      The buyer generally enters into the commodity purchase contract directly with the supplier. Bergkraft
      enters into a separate procurement services agreement with the buyer. The contractual and export
      responsibilities are agreed for each transaction.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .side { grid-column: 1 / span 5; }
  .side :global(.head) { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--header-h) + 3rem); }
  .steps { grid-column: 7 / -1; }
  li {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7.5rem) 1fr; gap: var(--s-5);
    padding-block: var(--s-6); border-top: 1px solid var(--c-line);
  }
  li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-line); }
  .num {
    font-family: var(--f-serif); font-weight: 300; font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 2rem + 3vw, 4.75rem); line-height: 0.9;
    color: transparent; -webkit-text-stroke: 1px var(--c-brass); transition: color var(--dur) var(--ease);
  }
  li.is-visible .num, li:hover .num { color: var(--c-brass); }
  li div { display: grid; gap: var(--s-3); }
  .out { font-size: var(--t-sm); }
  .out span { font-size: var(--t-xs); letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--c-brass-deep); margin-right: 0.6em; }
  .clar { grid-column: 7 / -1; margin-top: var(--s-7); }

  @media (max-width: 62rem) {
    .side, .steps, .clar { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .side :global(.head) { position: static; }
  }
</style>
